# Concierge — Twelve-Factor environment overrides (template).
#
# USAGE:
#   cp .env.example .env        # gitignored
#   $EDITOR .env                # fill in the values you need
#   docker compose up           # Compose auto-loads .env into the gateway
#
# Anything left blank or commented out is simply not exported into the
# gateway's process environment. config/gateway*.yaml uses ${VAR} /
# ${VAR:-default} placeholders, which load_config() expands from this env at
# startup. A ${VAR} with no default that is unset is a startup ERROR —
# secrets cannot silently fall back to a literal placeholder.
#
# NEVER commit a populated .env. The whole file is gitignored (.gitignore
# has: .env, .env.*). The committed template below contains only the names
# and what they're for.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret configuration (uncomment to override)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream MCP server credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are referenced from config/gateway*.yaml headers: ${BM_LIVE_TOKEN},
# ${NOTES_TOKEN}, ${JIRA_TOKEN}, etc. Add or remove entries to match the
# upstreams you actually use. Any value can be a literal token or pulled
# from a secret manager via a wrapper script that sets the env var before
# invoking `docker compose up`.
#
# BridgeMind remote MCP (referenced by config/gateway.yaml when present)
# BM_LIVE_TOKEN=
#
# Notes / Streamable HTTP example upstream (referenced by gateway.example.yaml)
# NOTES_TOKEN=
#
# Jira / legacy SSE example upstream (referenced by gateway.example.yaml)
# JIRA_TOKEN=
